ref 17592186120724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1045 "The Shortest Distance Between a Plane and a Point" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1050 960.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120020 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e15d96c3-59f3-5ea3-8c30-d6c68ac605ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120251 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120251 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120251 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120251 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3,5,-2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120251 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f22d111-9bd0-53c0-9506-a867aa25de4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120251 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(5,9,0).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8-8|}{\\sqrt{4+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120724 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120724 #edb/ref 1061 17940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120724 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9e02b271-c1ce-518a-b549-4e83a2061ea7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120724 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120725 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120725 #edb/ref 1061 17941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120725 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3779ed6b-358c-5101-8bd7-9de56abc2ade" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120725 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120726 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120726 #edb/ref 1061 17942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120726 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "213ff9e2-fe7a-528b-b535-4cf580c6aca9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120726 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120727 #edb/ref 1061 17943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120727 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdb4920a-a24d-544c-bdef-93ed800bfdd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120727 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121054 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to find the shortest distance between the point $P(3,0,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ that is given by the equation \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r}-\\langle 2 , 3 , 1 \\rangle ) \\cdot \\langle 4 , 4 , 2 \\rangle = 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, note that $\\mathbf{n} = \\langle 4 , 4 , 2 \\rangle$ is a vector that's normal to the plane.\n\n![](images/7b/7b2dfcd87c1f5e4e2c2b1a0b9a7f73899772e33e1020465b2b38d1b2de29a66c.png)\n\nLet's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,3,1)$. Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,1⟩-⟨3,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe shortest distance $d$ from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/26/26e494eef47db4dba3ac36dfa96c7e9a9d191321b22bb82874f3e74bbd7116ef.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+12+6|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|14|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is $\\dfrac{7}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121054 #edb/ref 1065 3261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121054 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "224c4104-9097-5a92-9c37-5d0fe22171a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121054 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260269 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260269 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260269 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c1bcf37-bd86-518e-aede-5addbc97699f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260642 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{13}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260642 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260642 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59b5fe8c-5178-580c-8f7a-66873832ec9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260727 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260727 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260727 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "62c4eecf-296e-5516-b53c-79b78ea2b9ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261036 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261036 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175921860