ref 17592186262053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262449 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b38b182d-b8bf-588a-b715-8c9ecc4e2585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186261477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262470 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bf6fc720-45dd-52de-b923-8c3e0a788e5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262937 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262937 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129095" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262937 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262937 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262937 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aec3d295-8d51-5dda-ba42-3f14845dd36d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262937 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,-1,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6-4|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-22|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262938 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262938 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129096" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262938 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262938 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,1,4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨3,-2,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,4,-4⟩=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262938 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "207cee96-48ff-5895-931d-4abf12241582" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262938 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(3,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-2,1⟩-⟨-3,1,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262940 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262940 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262940 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262940 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "997f5746-6279-5d4c-b439-ed85502108fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262940 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262959 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262959 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262959 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262959 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,2,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x+2y-4z=18.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262959 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "091a2bf6-b258-57c8-a9fa-cfb6d9f29751" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262959 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2y-4z & =18 \\\\ 4(2)+2(1)-4z & =18 \\\\ -4z & =8 \\\\ z & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,1,-2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,-2⟩-⟨-7,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,2,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|9\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36-2+20|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|54|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{6} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305240 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{22}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305240 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305240 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a111ed5-0950-5f80-a305-b88ed9c600f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305574 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305574 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305574 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c60338e-01a1-5dee-8591-c336fa874093" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305606 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305606 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305606 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "301af7be-9990-5644-a09f-8591c11e190d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305740 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305740 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305740 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d434f72-d817-5ecc-ac32-f306d8348871" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305886 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305886 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1