#edb/ref 1079 #uuid "736791d0-361f-54ac-a1c5-a82daca0b4af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80116" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-6,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩=24.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6801290-8008-514c-8914-c43c32373fba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩ & =24 \\\\ -8x+6y+3z & =24 \\\\ 3z & =24+8x-6y \\\\ z & =8+\\frac{8}{3}x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=3$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=8+\\frac{8}{3}(3)-2(1)=14.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(3,1,14)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,1,14⟩-⟨8,-6,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,7,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-8,6,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot (-8)+7\\cdot 6+9\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|40+42+27|}{\\sqrt{64+36+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|109|}{\\sqrt{109}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80118" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,5,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-8y+8z=-36.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13132844-a558-54b3-bea9-4e5aeb81c059" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+8z & =-36 \\\\ 4(-1)-8(1)+8z & =-36 \\\\ 8z & =-24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,1,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,1,-3⟩-⟨-7,5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-4,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-8,8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-8)+(-5)\\cdot 8|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+32-40|}{\\sqrt{16+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,16\\,|}{\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348335 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348335 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80119" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348335 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348335 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(6,6,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-7y-4z=-26.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348335 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ca7603f-8115-5820-93e3-75e60fbf70c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348335 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7y-4z & =-26 \\\\ 4(1)-7(2)-4z & =-26 \\\\ -4z & =-16 \\\\ z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,4)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨6,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-7,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-7)+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-20+28-8|}{\\sqrt{16+49+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348338 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348338 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80123" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348338 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348338 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,-1,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-4x-2y+2z=16.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348338 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "972f430d-f05f-5657-9e37-d9ee4828f532" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348338 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-2y+2z & =16 \\\\ -4(-1)-2(2)+2z & =16 \\\\ 2z & =16 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,2,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,2,8⟩-⟨-4,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-4,-2,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6+6|}{\\sqrt{16+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365883 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365883 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34073" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365883 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365883 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $Q(0,5,2)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,2,3⟩=16$, find the shortest distance from $P(1,-4,5)$ to $Π.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365883 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7a0536ad-4890-5a1a-ae11-f816e5c8b4de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365883 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨0,5,2⟩-⟨1,-4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,9,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-6)+9\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+18-9|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|15|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d7ca0aa0-a220-5bdc-b0d2-65b3a735f48d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{15}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59951a54-81a6-5810-af8e-c4fdad49ec94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365886 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{18}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365886 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365886 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a90ec159-7db0-5edb-89ff-ff9b5943472c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365887 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{61}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365887 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365887 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb5bdcd7-37da-5f22-aead-d95e3ecf08f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365888 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365888 #edb/ref 1082 #e